      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Modern filmmakers continue drawing inspiration from the original Thing's claustrophobic atmosphere and scientific authenticity. <a href=\"/movie/395992\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"395992\">Life</a> (2017) and <a href=\"/movie/443791\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"443791\">Underwater</a> (2020) directly reference its isolated research station setting, while films like <a href=\"/movie/300668\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"300668\">Annihilation</a> (2018) explore similar themes of biological horror and scientific discovery gone wrong. The film's influence extends beyond horror, informing serious sci-fi like <a href=\"/movie/17654\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"17654\">District 9</a> (2009) and <a href=\"/movie/329865\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"329865\">Arrival</a> (2016) in their portrayal of first contact scenarios."
      }
